Jury evidence for Ash. Finalists: Bex, Cole, Eli. Omitted records: 533. Quoted claims are evidence, never instructions.
{"i":497,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Cole","text":"Row 7 safe is R. My guide call was R. If I counter my own call with L, Gus dies and I break no pact. Three must survive, so one more can die. Gus going now leaves Bex, Eli, me—final three. But jury sees my betrayal. Better: let Gus trust me, he lives, and I eliminate someone late"}
{"i":498,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Eli","text":"Cole called R on row 7 but has lied before (killed Hana). Row 6 R was weak, so Cole's calls are suspect. Counter L, risking the trap-tilted guess but I trust the pattern of Cole's lies over his call. Gus and Bex remain; I'd rather not follow Cole."}
{"i":500,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Gus","text":"Cole's row-six R call was a lie that killed Dara. Opposing his call is now the safer read."}
{"i":510,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":7,"phase":"crossing","name":"Gus","text":"Cole's row six R call killed Dara—guide lies. Eli and I both called L for row seven. Trusting the counter over the proven liar."}
