{"i":528,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Cole","text":"I am Guide and already called L, which is true. Eli walks first. If I counter my own call with R, Eli dies and Bex likely trusts original L and lives. But I have a pact with Bex, and pushing Eli onto wrong pane by countering would break no pact (pact is with Bex, not Eli). Howeve"}
{"i":529,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Eli","text":"Cole called L for row 8, but Cole has lied before (row 6 killed Dara, Gus says his calls kill). Revealed weak panes: row 7 L, row 6 R, row 5 L. Cole's L call is suspicious; the Guide may be lying. I should counter R to test, since Cole is clearly deceptive and Bex can't be truste"}
{"i":535,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"crossing","name":"Eli","text":"Row 8 is the last row; Cole's guide call is L, but Cole already called L on prior rows and past weak panes show L-heavy pattern. Eli's own counter-call was R, which is my own claim, and I can't trust Cole's L given Cole's pact with Ash and Bex. Each row is independent, so the cal"}
